5      3      5         95     20      0    142   3    2     389    0        1        1      5
6      4     31        126      0      0    160   3  400     166    0        1        1      6

Notice that all transect surveys where no detections were made are removed and that the check.data() function has been used to prepare the data for a covariate distance detection function (giving the last 3 columns)

my process for model selection is to first check the best performing key function based on AIC with formula ~1 (no covariates). Then to begin testing the influence of various covariates, if the inclusion of a covariate gives the same of greater AIC, I leave that covariate out of the model for that species.
This has led me to this model structure below as an example for buffalo:

buf.df<-ddf(method="ds"
            , dsmodel =~mcds(key="hn"
            , formula=~scale(Group3)+scale(Group1)+scale(size)+VEG,  adj.series="poly", adj.order=2)
            , data=fxddd[[1]]$data
            , meta.data=list(width=450)
            , control=list(optimx.maxit=10000
            , refit=TRUE, refits=1000, nrefits=1000, estimate=T, silent=F, debug=T))

## Truncation distance was based on excluding all points from no covariate model with detection
## probability less than 0.15 giving observations with distances =<450

check.mono(buf.df)
