> Here is where it gets sticky!
>
> I find that the values in bufvars$eswf.fitted confusing. The help file states "it returns integral 0-W p(y)*pi(y) where pi(y)=1/W for lines..." and using the last observation as an example this can be reproduced 208.7/450=0.464.  But what does this value represent? Is it actually the probability that a buffalo herd is detected given the values of the covariates for that observation?
>
> In other words, using the last observation again as an example, would all observations in a transect with the following values:
>
> Group1=0
> Group3=0
> VEG=2
> size=2
>
> have a detection probability of 0.46 using the predict function? If so, does this mean that I can use the predict function and my detection function model to give the probability of detecting a herd of buffalo in any transect once the values for these variables are known? (Just to reiterate, this will provide a very useful variable to account for variation in a separate model).
>
> I would be grateful for any direction or correction in my understanding of anything here and perhaps any known examples where a similar thing has been done. Thank you for your time!!
>
